# Environments

Every env implements:

- `reset(seed: int | None = None) -> (obs, info)`
- `step(action) -> (obs, reward, terminated, truncated, info)`
- `legal_moves() -> list[int]`
- `info` always includes `legal_moves` (and usually `n_legal`)

Shared types: `EnvState`, `RoundResult` (see `environments/tic_tac_toe.py` and RPS+).

## Rules

- Same seed must produce the same trajectory.
- Illegal actions raise `ValueError` (RPS+ included; smoke-test future games may document fallbacks).
- Register new envs in `environments/__init__.py` and add rules to `environments/game_specs.py` when they appear in the dashboard.
- RPS+ only: import `BEST_COUNTER` from `environments/rps_plus.py`. Never define a local POWER counter map.
- Mirror patterns in `tests/test_environment.py` and `tests/test_future_games.py` when adding tests.
